Now, the first out of the program will be an exhibition of fancy roping and riding by Bill Martin's boys.

00:47:50.730 --> 00:47:55.880
it can be. Oh, don't worry, Dad. He'll be here. Well, I hope he gets here soon.

00:48:09.980 --> 00:48:12.900
I wonder what I can get for this piece of glass in a hawk shop.

00:48:13.340 --> 00:48:16.320
You'll get a good sock in the jaw when I get loose.

00:50:18.610 --> 00:50:19.210
Well, did you get him?

00:50:19.470 --> 00:50:21.260
I'll say we got him.

00:50:21.340 --> 00:50:22.160
Where is he?

00:50:22.260 --> 00:50:24.180
That old shack down near Tuttle Creek Ranch.

00:50:24.400 --> 00:50:25.490
We tied him up.

00:50:25.610 --> 00:50:27.450
And I left Denver there watching.

00:50:29.220 --> 00:50:29.700
Okay, Chief.

00:51:15.324 --> 00:51:15.624
Thank you.

00:52:10.170 --> 00:52:11.570
I'm going to make another little announcement.

00:52:12.530 --> 00:52:19.080
It's nigh on to 3 o'clock, and we're going to start the big event of the day, the relay race.

00:52:19.510 --> 00:52:21.330
Boys, bring on your horses.

00:52:22.170 --> 00:52:23.070
I'm worried about Ted.

00:52:26.340 --> 00:52:28.900
Taking a little exercise, are you?

00:52:30.030 --> 00:52:31.430
Do you good. Go ahead, boy.

00:52:49.020 --> 00:52:56.680
Jack, Peggy, all right, get your rope.

00:53:12.800 --> 00:53:15.060
Saturday, tell me you're a pretty good rider.

00:53:16.770 --> 00:53:20.570
Well, sorry, but there's no race for you today.

00:54:21.560 --> 00:54:22.900
Has the race started yet?

00:54:24.120 --> 00:54:25.380
Has it worked fast?

00:54:27.900 --> 00:54:29.660
Judge Newshead!

00:54:31.790 --> 00:54:33.310
I don't know. I haven't seen him, Judge.

00:54:33.680 --> 00:54:34.840
Gosh, that's the funny thing.

00:54:34.940 --> 00:54:37.100
We ought to be here by now. It's time to start the race.

00:54:40.280 --> 00:54:41.360
How'd you know I was here?

00:54:41.520 --> 00:54:42.940
Well, we'll tell you all about it later.

00:54:43.310 --> 00:54:46.440
You've got a race for you.

00:54:47.300 --> 00:54:48.620
All right. Thanks, Peggy.

00:55:35.080 --> 00:55:35.440
Hold ya.

00:56:07.800 --> 00:56:11.720
Hey, Martin, where's your rider? We're ready to start this race.

00:56:12.020 --> 00:56:13.940
Well, he'll be here soon, Judge.

00:56:14.220 --> 00:56:17.320
Well, if he ain't here in a hurry, you better get yourself another rider.

00:56:31.790 --> 00:56:32.010
People.

00:57:11.460 --> 00:57:16.840
I can't imagine what happened to Ted. I guess we haven't got a chance.

00:57:30.570 --> 00:57:34.900
Henning, you've got to ride this race for us.

00:57:36.900 --> 00:57:37.360
Right, boss.

00:57:52.350 --> 00:57:55.960
Hey, judge, come stand now.

00:57:56.040 --> 00:57:56.980
Here comes Ted.

01:00:33.420 --> 01:00:36.370
Ted, you rode a great race, boy.

01:00:37.170 --> 01:00:39.740
You certainly had me worried.

01:00:40.280 --> 01:00:40.940
What happened to you?

01:00:41.450 --> 01:00:44.200
Well, they framed me, boss.

01:00:44.960 --> 01:00:48.080
I'll tell you about it later.

01:01:01.780 --> 01:01:15.000
This is what I went into town for, dear.

01:01:21.040 --> 01:01:21.900
Hope it fits you.

01:01:35.720 --> 01:01:36.240
is your son.

01:02:01.590 --> 01:02:03.770
I'm a granddadder, no.
